  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 1215 AM MDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nQuiet conditions are on tap Saturday night. On Sunday, the upper \nhigh over the Four Corners will strengthen slightly to 592dam, but\ntemperatures will vary only slightly from Saturday. Northeast to \neast winds will increase as another back door front slides through\nthe area and easterly synoptic flow strengthens as well. At H7, a\n30kt jet streak is noted roughly along the I-40 corridor. Expect \nwinds to pick up during the late morning hours with surface wind \ngusts near 25-35 mph across central and west central NM, to \ninclude ABQ, in the aftn. Winds will decrease around sunset. \n\nMonday continues to look quiet, though the upper high will \nweaken. There's a small chance of a shower or storm across the \nsouth central mountains, but confidence is low that will occur. \nDry conditions elsewhere with high temperatures near or just below\nseasonal normals. \n\nModels are in better agreement this morning that the shortwave\nthat crosses NM on Tuesday and Wednesday will be quite weak, and \nwill produce little, if any, precipitation. Greatest chances for \nany light precipitation will be across the northern mountains on\nTuesday. Rather, it looks like temperatures will continue to\nclimb. All areas will be near to above normal both days. An upper\nhigh will build into the area on Thursday, keeping temperatures at\nor above normal.",
